      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1667557537,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Is calling 'sorted' here so that files are examined in alphabetical order.\n\nWhen we iterate the set, are the files coming back in this same order?  If so, then don't need sorted call here.\n\nI think examining files in sorted order servers 2 purposes:\n\n- if the checking is slow (and there is enough output), you can tell at a glance how far through the directory the scan is\n\n- if you want to compare with previous output, it is helpful to see it in the same order\n\nThese 2 considerations apply less to check_tfs.py than to some of the other checks (quick, and little output).  Some googling suggests that python sets by default have random hashes.  De-duplicating the list of files could be useful though.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
