      "title": "check_tfs.py: use a set for the files to be checked",
      "message": "check_tfs.py: use a set for the files to be checked\n\nUse a set instead of a list for the files that we'll check, both in the\nis_dissector_file function and in the \"main function\".\n\nBy definition, a set does not support multiple identical entries. We can\nsimply add file names without having to check for duplicates.\n\nWhen using a list, we store the file names in alphabetical order. This\nmeans that we also process the files in alphabetical order. The caller\ncan tell from the current file name how far we are in the checks. When\nwe use a set, the entries have no defined order. We sort the entries\nbefore we print or process them to keep the alphabetical order.\n",
      "author_name": "Martin Kaiser",
      "author_email": "wireshark@kaiser.cx",
      "authored_date": "2023-11-22T20:59:36.000+03:00",
